  "description": "KIFTUR crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C91 H131 Ag16 Cl1 F24 O26 P3 Yb3,C1 H4 O1,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Ag1 (Ag) has 1 O neighbors; Ag2 (Ag) has 2 O neighbors; Ag3 (Ag) has 0 O neighbors; Ag4 (Ag) has 0 O neighbors; Ag5 (Ag) has 1 O neighbors; Ag6 (Ag) has 1 O neighbors; Ag7 (Ag) has 1 O neighbors; Ag8 (Ag) has 1 O neighbors; Ag9 (Ag) has 0 O neighbors; Ag10 (Ag) has 3 O neighbors; Ag11 (Ag) has 3 O neighbors; Ag12 (Ag) has 3 O neighbors; Ag13 (Ag) has 1 O neighbors; Ag14 (Ag) has 1 O neighbors; Ag15 (Ag) has 2 O neighbors; Ag16 (Ag) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 8 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.065-4.070 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 72.46-119.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H133Ag16ClF24O28P3Yb3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
